(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[14 1 "// The module _signal (PY6f; Modules/signalmodule.c): the process's signals delivered to Python handlers."] [15 1 "// signal(n, callable) has os/signal notify one channel; its receiver goroutine marks the signal pending (the C"] [16 1 "// handler's trip_signal), sets the eval breaker, wakes the main thread when it blocks and writes the wakeup fd;"] [17 1 "// the main thread runs the handlers at its next check (thread_gil.go). SIG_IGN is signal.Ignore, SIG_DFL"] [18 1 "// signal.Reset. raise_signal and os.kill of the own process run the handler before they return, as on Linux."] [19 1 "// The interval timers (alarm, setitimer) are Go timers sending the signal; pthread_sigmask's mask is kept here:"] [20 1 "// a blocked signal stays pending (sigpending, sigwait) until unblocked."] [26 1 "// sysPidfdSendSignal is pidfd_send_signal's syscall number (424 on linux/amd64 and linux/arm64)"] [31 39 "// the main thread's wake-up from a blocking wait"] [32 39 "// any arrival (sigwait)"] [33 39 "// tripped, its handler to run"] [34 39 "// is_tripped"] [35 39 "// pthread_sigmask's mask"] [36 39 "// arrived while blocked (sigpending)"] [37 39 "// notified on sigCh"] [38 39 "// arrivals so far (pidfd_send_signal's wait)"] [39 39 "// set_wakeup_fd's fd, -1 none"] [41 2 "// sigHandlers are the Python-level handlers (Handlers[n].func), touched under the GIL"] [43 21 "// default_int_handler"] [48 2 "// SIGPIPE and SIGXFSZ ignored at the start, before any import of signal, as CPython's _PySignal_Init does with"] [49 2 "// install_signal_handlers (py-design-1122: a write to a closed pipe is a BrokenPipeError, json.tool's exit status"] [50 2 "// EPIPE, not the signal's death); _signal's import records them as SIG_IGN"] [54 1 "// blockedMask is pthread_sigmask's mask as a kernel sigset (py-mp-1125): a child started by ForkExec (fork_exec,"] [55 1 "// posix_spawn without setsigmask, spawnv) gets it, as a C process's child inherits its thread's mask."] [66 1 "// startSignals starts the receiver once."] [79 1 "// ownSignalHook, when set, handles a signal pyi sends itself (killSignal of its own pid, raise_signal) before the"] [80 1 "// signal module does (queue 220: faulthandler's handlers, and the default action that ends the process): handled true"] [81 1 "// and the call returns."] [84 1 "// signalTakenHook, when set, says a signal's handler is another module's (queue 220: faulthandler.register without"] [85 1 "// chain replaces the Python handler, as its sigaction does): the Python handler is not tripped."] [88 1 "// deliverSignal is the C handler: held when blocked, else tripped; the wakeup fd written."] [110 1 "// ExtRaiseSignal is raise(sig) of C code in pyi's C world (arbace/pyctypes; queue 594: _testcapi's"] [111 1 "// raise_SIGINT_then_send_None) for a signal the C world left at its default action: the process's signals are"] [112 1 "// Python's, so a signal with a Python handler is delivered as the kernel runs CPython's C handler inside raise (the"] [113 1 "// handler tripped, or held while blocked) and its Python handler runs at the next check, not before raise returns;"] [114 1 "// false for any other signal (the C world's default action ends the process)."] [119 33 "// musl's raise is tkill"] [124 1 "// tripSignal marks n pending and wakes the main thread (trip_signal)."] [136 1 "// runPendingSignals is _PyErr_CheckSignalsTstate on the main thread: each tripped signal's Python handler"] [137 1 "// called with the signal and the running frame; an exception from one leaves the rest tripped for later."] [168 1 "// setOSHandler makes the process's action for n follow its Python handler and the mask: notified when a"] [169 1 "// callable handles it or it is blocked, else ignored or the default."] [193 3 "// SIG_DFL is the default action, also for a signal ignored at the start that Go's Reset leaves ignored"] [194 3 "// (py-mods-1122)"] [201 1 "// exitSigint is Modules/main.c's exit_sigint after an unhandled KeyboardInterrupt (queue 231): SIGINT's default action"] [202 1 "// restored and the signal sent to the process, so that its parent sees it killed by SIGINT; else exit status 130."] [208 38 "// delivered to this thread on the call's return; another one's at the latest here"] [213 1 "// killSignal is kill(pid, sig). The own process's signal with a Python handler, not blocked, is delivered here"] [214 1 "// and its handler run before kill returns, as the kernel delivers it to the calling thread before kill returns"] [215 1 "// (and SIGPROF, which Go's runtime keeps for itself, reaches the handler)."] [230 3 "// blocked: pending when kill returns, as the kernel makes it (queue 231: sigpending right after saw nothing, the"] [231 3 "// signal still on its way through Go's handler thread)"] [241 1 "// the interval timers (ITIMER_REAL, ITIMER_VIRTUAL, ITIMER_PROF), counted in wall time"] [255 1 "// setItimer arms which's timer (value 0 disarms), returning the old value and interval."] [274 3 "// disarmed: an expiry not yet handled is dropped, as the kernel's single pending bit is taken by the"] [275 3 "// handler that disarms it"] [296 5 "// a Python handler: delivered here, under the timer's lock, so a disarmed timer sends no more"] [297 5 "// (and SIGPROF, which Go's runtime keeps for itself, reaches it)"] [326 2 "// the start installs SIGINT's handler (py-os-1124; pylifecycle's init_signals, _PySignal_Init: a program that never"] [327 2 "// imports signal ends with KeyboardInterrupt at a SIGINT, not by the signal; test_subprocess's test_send_signal)"] [348 4 "// as at CPython's start: SIGINT's default_int_handler, SIGPIPE and SIGXFSZ ignored, the rest SIG_DFL"] [354 4 "// a SIGHUP ignored at the process's start (nohup, a parent's SIG_IGN): SIG_IGN, as CPython's signal_get_set_handlers"] [355 4 "// reads it (py-mods-1122)"] [360 4 "// SIGINT's default_int_handler, unless the process started with SIGINT ignored (signal_install_handlers sets it"] [361 4 "// only over SIG_DFL: a child of nohup or of a SIG_IGN keeps ignoring it)"] [481 5 "// the C handler runs inside raise(): the Python handler before raise_signal returns"] [504 4 "// set_wakeup_fd(fd, /, *, warn_on_full_buffer=True)"] [613 5 "// only the main thread runs handlers: wait for any arrival"] [617 4 "// until a signal is pending (a stale wake-up token is not one)"] [670 7 "// delivered on unblocking: the default action or nothing"] [729 5 "// the own process's signal (a pidfd of another process times out here, harmlessly) handled"] [730 5 "// before the call returns, as the kernel delivers it"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[51 82] [58 12] [58 22] [71 35] [105 26] [146 12] [146 22] [159 60] [189 22] [218 40] [235 50] [350 14] [350 24] [398 31] [413 14] [413 24] [415 39] [440 40] [462 26] [476 40] [487 63] [523 37] [540 32] [555 31] [597 37] [646 14] [646 24] [675 40] [717 35] [725 104] [732 16] [732 61]]} (go/file "builtins_signal.go" :imports [


